@MicrosoftLearn • On-prem = you handle everything 
• IaaS / PaaS = provider handles hardware; you manage apps & data 
• SaaS = provider handles everything; you just pay overpriced bill (for logs especially ) 😜

@MicrosoftLearn 83% of enterprises plan to deploy agentic AI, but only 29% say they're ready to secure it. 

A single compromised agent with shared API keys can poison 87% of downstream decisions in under 4 hours. 

The infrastructure was always the moat now it's also the attack surface.

@MicrosoftLearn 100% this.

AI agents are only as reliable as what's underneath them.

Bad permissions, zero logging, weak APIs? Your agent fails silently and no one knows why until it's too late.

@MicrosoftLearn Security becomes even more important.
An agent with access to APIs is essentially an automated user with privileges.
Without proper scoping, one compromised prompt can turn into a full system compromise.

@MicrosoftLearn Exactly

AI is just the interface, infra is the backbone.

That’s where @fluence_project comes in providing decentralized compute, verifiable infra with no single point of failure.

@MicrosoftLearn Azure security modules dropping like: 

Key Vault → 'secrets? what secrets' Managed identities → 'passwords are for boomers' App Configuration → 'settings? we don’t do settings, we do ✨vibes✨'

App now bulletproof 😎

@MicrosoftLearn Azure Databricks Lakehouse processes 10 PB data daily. 

India's AI infra spend: $5.2B this FY. 

Fabric + OneLake cuts ETL 70% productivity edge for Nifty IT pack amid crash.

@MicrosoftLearn Most people wait to understand everything first.

The real path is: touch it → break it → rebuild it.

Clarity comes after contact.

