@MicrosoftLearn been there with Claude prompts for People Loop

now I just test one thing, see if it breaks, ship it if it works

the best prompt is the one you actually use tomorrow

@MicrosoftLearn you can often break a plateau by getting the agent to outline a task for another, and then output what it expects to see. 
1. Flipping from 'What does the user need' to 'how do i understand this really so I can formally describe the mechanics/method/... to another?" is a coherent hand-off.
2. If it differs, the hindsight can be what it needs

